  <g font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">
    <text x="32" y="43" font-size="22" fill="#72e5df" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">01 / FICTIONAL SCENARIO</text>
    <text x="32" y="91" font-size="31" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">The value of a cut</text>
    <text x="32" y="129" font-size="31" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">depends on timing</text>
    <text x="32" y="174" font-size="24" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Same cut: 2 cents per litre</text>
    <text x="32" y="209" font-size="24" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Contribution over one hour</text>
    <text x="32" y="267" font-size="23" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Original price</text>
    <text x="448" y="267" font-size="29" fill="#7e94ad" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">€100.00</text>
    <rect x="32" y="285" width="300" height="24" rx="3" fill="#7e94ad" />
    <text x="32" y="363" font-size="23" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Match after 60 min</text>
    <text x="448" y="363" font-size="29" fill="#72e5df" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">€120.00</text>
    <rect x="32" y="381" width="360" height="24" rx="3" fill="#72e5df" />
    <text x="32" y="459" font-size="23" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">Match after 1 min</text>
    <text x="448" y="459" font-size="29" fill="#f2c875" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">€80.67</text>
    <rect x="32" y="477" width="242.0" height="24" rx="3" fill="#f2c875" />
    <line x1="32" y1="517" x2="422" y2="517" stroke="#b8c8db" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <line x1="32" y1="517" x2="32" y2="524" stroke="#b8c8db" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="32" y="548" font-size="22" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
    <line x1="182" y1="517" x2="182" y2="524" stroke="#b8c8db" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="182" y="548" font-size="22" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">50</text>
    <line x1="332" y1="517" x2="332" y2="524" stroke="#b8c8db" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="332" y="548" font-size="22" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">100</text>
    <line x1="422" y1="517" x2="422" y2="524" stroke="#b8c8db" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="422" y="548" font-size="22" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="middle">130</text>
    <rect x="24" y="581" width="432" height="105" rx="10" fill="#181d25" />
    <text x="40" y="619" font-size="25" fill="#f0f4fa" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start">Scenario threshold: 30 min</text>
    <text x="40" y="655" font-size="24" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">to recover the original €100</text>
    <text x="32" y="718" font-size="21" fill="#b8c8db" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start">l0g · Fictional figures · 17 Sep 2026</text>
  </g>
</svg>
<figcaption>Figure 1. Fictional calculation over a fixed 60-minute window. Contribution after the assumed variable cost, before other expenses. Until the rival matches, sales rise from 1,000 to 1,500 litres per hour; they then return to 1,000. Costs are unchanged. Source: l0g calculations, 17 September 2026. This is not a market-equilibrium simulation.</figcaption>
</figure>
)}

